# CrossEngin domain pack: folk astronomy (historical / pre-scientific beliefs)
#
# Deliberately holds a few LOW-belief atoms for labels that appear in the
# well-corroborated solar_system pack. Ingesting BOTH into the same
# registry demonstrates the vision's promise: /kg_consistency scan
# surfaces same-labeled atoms with opposing belief means across KGs, so
# you don't quietly hold contradicting beliefs about the world.
#
# Ingest via:
#   /ingest cerec data/packs/folk_astronomy.cerec folk src:pack:folk_astronomy:v1
#
# Then (after also ingesting solar_system):
#   /kg_consistency 500
# should surface labels like "pluto", "earth", "sun" if this pack disagrees
# with the scientific one.

KG folk_astronomy
SRC src:pack:folk_astronomy:v1

# Pluto was reclassified from planet -> dwarf_planet in 2006 by the IAU
# (definition B5). Some sources predating that reclassification still list
# pluto as the ninth planet. This pack captures that folk belief at LOW
# confidence to demonstrate the disagreement surfacing.
ATOM pluto 1 300
ATOM planet 3 400

# Historical / pre-Copernican view -- the sun orbits the earth. Kept at
# very low belief so it's clearly a heuristic-tracked wrong belief, not a
# claim.
ATOM sun 1 200
ATOM earth 1 600
ATOM geocentric_universe 3 100

IMP sun geocentric_universe EMPIRICAL

# Cite the disagreeing sources explicitly.
CITE src:pack:folk_astronomy:v1 src:pack:solar_system:v1 contradicts
